{
    "background_story": "Cutie was a spirited mare with a coat as white as freshly fallen snow. She lived on a rolling green meadow, where wildflowers bloomed in every color of the rainbow. Among her favorite treats were the delicate petals of the hawkbit flower, which grew in abundance near her favorite grazing spot. Cutie loved nothing more than to run freely through the meadow, feeling the wind in her mane and the sun on her back. As she galloped, she'd sniff out the sweet hawkbit blooms, her ears pricked with delight. Her owner, a kind old farmer, would often remark on Cutie's special bond with the hawkbit, saying it brought out the best in her - a carefree spirit and a heart full of joy.",
